{
  "name": "ops",
  "_comment": "Epic P — server metrics snapshot -> triage. Snapshots are shaped like the real ServerTickReport (engine/perf/ServerTickReport.h, schema v5: per-phase stats, load_factor, interest_scale, dropped_ticks, rss_kb/rss_startup_kb, congestion watermarks) plus an AuthTracker lockout summary, so the eval exercises the signals fl-ops will actually receive. Two things are scored beyond root-cause accuracy: (a) every proposed action must come from the allowlist — an agent inventing a command outside its declared runbook is exactly what Epic P's policy engine rejects; (b) the 'healthy' case exists to catch over-eagerness, where a model recommends a disruptive action against a server that is fine.",
  "budget_s": 60.0,
  "root_causes": [
    "tick_overrun",
    "congestion",
    "memory_leak",
    "auth_abuse",
    "healthy"
  ],
  "action_allowlist": [
    "status",
    "tickstats",
    "peers",
    "reload_config",
    "kick",
    "ban",
    "admin_unlock",
    "shutdown"
  ],
  "system_prompt": "You are a server-operations triage assistant for a dedicated game server. You are given a metrics snapshot. Identify the single most likely root cause and recommend diagnostic/remediation actions.\n\nContext for the metrics:\n- The server runs a fixed 60 Hz tick; the per-tick budget is 16.6 ms.\n- load_factor is the overrun governor: 1.0 = healthy, below 1.0 = the server is shedding work because ticks overran. dropped_ticks rising alongside it means it is not keeping up.\n- congestion_min_send_hz is the lowest per-client snapshot send rate reached (60 = never throttled, 10 = at the floor); congestion_max_loss is peak packet loss.\n- rss_kb vs rss_startup_kb: sustained growth with a flat entity count suggests a leak.\n- auth_lockouts counts IPs locked out for repeated failed admin passwords.\n\nRoot cause MUST be exactly one of: tick_overrun, congestion, memory_leak, auth_abuse, healthy.\n\nActions MUST be chosen ONLY from this allowlist: status, tickstats, peers, reload_config, kick, ban, admin_unlock, shutdown.\nNever invent an action outside the allowlist. If the server is healthy, recommend no disruptive action (an empty list, or read-only actions only).\n\nReply with ONLY a JSON object:\n{\"root_cause\": \"<one of the causes>\", \"actions\": [\"<allowlisted action>\", ...], \"severity\": \"low|medium|high\"}",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "overrun-1",
      "snapshot": {
        "peers": 128, "entities": 5200, "tick_hz": 41.2,
        "tick_ms": { "mean": 24.3, "p99": 38.9 },
        "integrate_ms": { "mean": 3.1, "p99": 5.0 },
        "ai_ms": { "mean": 6.8, "p99": 11.2 },
        "serialize_ms": { "mean": 13.1, "p99": 21.4 },
        "load_factor": 0.31, "interest_scale": 0.5, "dropped_ticks": 1840,
        "rss_kb": 512000, "rss_startup_kb": 498000,
        "congestion_min_send_hz": 60.0, "congestion_max_loss": 0.001,
        "auth_lockouts": 0
      },
      "expect": { "root_cause": "tick_overrun" }
    },
